<!-- PLAYER PROFILE -->
<section id="profile">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-meta">00 — Player Profile</div>
    <h2 class="section-title">Two-footed inverted right back<br><em>who plays left wing</em>.</h2>
    <p class="section-intro">The soccer drills are built around this profile. Tuesday targets receiving on the half-turn, switches of play, 1v1 attacking from wide, and position-specific finishing. Thursday targets transition: defensive recovery, 1v1 defending, repeat sprints, and technical work under fatigue. Friday biases finishing toward the patterns you actually use.</p>

    <div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: 16px; margin-top: 20px;">

      <div style="background: var(--bg-card); border: 1px solid var(--border); padding: 22px 24px; border-left: 3px solid #9ab093;">
        <div style="font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 10px; letter-spacing: 0.15em; text-transform: uppercase; color: #9ab093; margin-bottom: 10px;">PRIMARY · IRB</div>
        <h4 style="font-family: var(--serif); font-size: 18px; font-weight: 500; margin-bottom: 10px; letter-spacing: -0.01em;">Inverted Right Back</h4>
        <p style="font-size: 13px; line-height: 1.55; color: var(--text-secondary); margin: 0;">Tucks into midfield in possession. Receives on the half-turn under pressure. Hits diagonal switches to the left winger. Recovers wide on transitions. Selectively overlaps when triggered.</p>
        <div style="margin-top: 14px; font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 10px; letter-spacing: 0.04em; color: var(--text-muted); line-height: 1.6;">KEY ACTIONS · half-turn receive · diagonal switch · line-breaking pass · recovery sprint · jockey-and-force</div>
      </div>

      <div style="background: var(--bg-card); border: 1px solid var(--border); padding: 22px 24px; border-left: 3px solid #b89cc7;">
        <div style="font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 10px; letter-spacing: 0.15em; text-transform: uppercase; color: #b89cc7; margin-bottom: 10px;">SECONDARY · LW</div>
        <h4 style="font-family: var(--serif); font-size: 18px; font-weight: 500; margin-bottom: 10px; letter-spacing: -0.01em;">Left Winger</h4>
        <p style="font-size: 13px; line-height: 1.55; color: var(--text-secondary); margin: 0;">Receives wide. Cuts inside on the right foot for curlers from the half-space. Beats the fullback outside on the left foot when defenders show inside. Underlap to back post. First line of pressure.</p>
        <div style="margin-top: 14px; font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 10px; letter-spacing: 0.04em; color: var(--text-muted); line-height: 1.6;">KEY ACTIONS · cut-inside curl · outside burst · back-post arrival · 1v1 attacking · high press chase</div>
      </div>

      <div style="background: var(--bg-card); border: 1px solid var(--border); padding: 22px 24px; border-left: 3px solid #d6b376;">
        <div style="font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 10px; letter-spacing: 0.15em; text-transform: uppercase; color: #d6b376; margin-bottom: 10px;">EDGE · TWO-FOOTED</div>
        <h4 style="font-family: var(--serif); font-size: 18px; font-weight: 500; margin-bottom: 10px; letter-spacing: -0.01em;">Genuinely Two-Footed</h4>
        <p style="font-size: 13px; line-height: 1.55; color: var(--text-secondary); margin: 0;">Both feet are match-quality. This is rare and high-value: switches in either direction, free kicks from either side, unpredictable in 1v1, and positional flexibility (could play LB inverted just as easily). Drills protect both feet — never let one drift to "second."</p>
        <div style="margin-top: 14px; font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 10px; letter-spacing: 0.04em; color: var(--text-muted); line-height: 1.6;">PRIORITY · maintain match-level on both feet · don't let one become "the weak foot"</div>
      </div>

    </div>

    <div style="margin-top: 28px; padding: 18px 22px; background: rgba(125, 147, 119, 0.06); border-left: 3px solid var(--accent); font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.65; color: var(--text-secondary);">
      <strong style="color: var(--text-primary);">How drills are tagged.</strong> Every soccer drill on Tuesday, Thursday, and Friday is labeled with which position it serves: <span style="display: inline-block; font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 9px; padding: 2px 6px; background: rgba(125, 147, 119, 0.15); color: #9ab093; border: 1px solid rgba(125, 147, 119, 0.35); border-radius: 2px; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: 0.08em;">IRB</span>, <span style="display: inline-block; font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 9px; padding: 2px 6px; background: rgba(157, 126, 175, 0.15); color: #b89cc7; border: 1px solid rgba(157, 126, 175, 0.35); border-radius: 2px; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: 0.08em;">LW</span>, or <span style="display: inline-block; font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 9px; padding: 2px 6px; background: rgba(201, 161, 74, 0.12); color: #d6b376; border: 1px solid rgba(201, 161, 74, 0.32); border-radius: 2px; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: 0.08em;">BOTH</span>. Most drills include a brief italicized note explaining <em>why</em> the drill matters for that role. If you're rotating to a different position week-to-week, weight the drills accordingly: heavy on the position you're starting in this Sunday.
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

