          <div class="drill-line"><div class="name"><strong>Light jog with ball</strong> · vary touches every 5 yards · both feet equal time<span class="pos-tags"><span class="pos both">BOTH</span></span><span class="why">Wakes up the touch on both feet — your two-footedness is your edge, maintain it daily.</span></div><div class="scheme">3 min</div></div>
          <div class="drill-line"><div class="name"><strong>Leg swings + lateral lunges</strong> · open hips for the cuts ahead<span class="pos-tags"><span class="pos both">BOTH</span></span></div><div class="scheme">2 min</div></div>
          <div class="drill-line"><div class="name"><strong>Toe-tap + V-cuts</strong> · close-control activation, both feet alternate<span class="pos-tags"><span class="pos both">BOTH</span></span></div><div class="scheme">3 × 30s</div></div>
          <div class="drill-line"><div class="name"><strong>A-skips → B-skips</strong> · 20 yards each<span class="pos-tags"><span class="pos both">BOTH</span></span></div><div class="scheme">2 × 20 yds</div></div>
        </div>

        <div class="session-block">
          <div class="block-head">
            <span class="block-num">BLOCK 02</span>
            <span class="block-title">Receiving on the Half-Turn</span>
            <span class="block-time">15 MIN</span>
          </div>
          <div class="drill-line"><div class="name"><strong>Open-body wall pass</strong> · receive with back foot, body opens 90°, return-pass with the same foot · 5 min each foot<span class="pos-tags"><span class="pos irb">IRB</span></span><span class="why">The single most important IRB skill — receiving in midfield with body already turned forward. If you can't do this under pressure, you can't play inverted.</span></div><div class="scheme">10 min</div></div>
          <div class="drill-line"><div class="name"><strong>Shoulder-check receive</strong> · before every touch, glance over shoulder, then receive · build it as a habit · use both feet<span class="pos-tags"><span class="pos both">BOTH</span></span><span class="why">Inverted RBs and wingers both need to know what's behind them BEFORE the ball arrives. Habit first, skill second.</span></div><div class="scheme">3 min</div></div>
          <div class="drill-line"><div class="name"><strong>Aerial control to set</strong> · throw ball up, control with chest/thigh, set up to switch with opposite foot<span class="pos-tags"><span class="pos irb">IRB</span></span></div><div class="scheme">2 min</div></div>
        </div>

        <div class="session-block">
          <div class="block-head">
            <span class="block-num">BLOCK 03</span>
            <span class="block-title">Switches + Line-Breaking Passes</span>
            <span class="block-time">12 MIN</span>
          </div>
          <div class="drill-line"><div class="name"><strong>Diagonal switch — right foot</strong> · 30-40 yard ball from right half-space to imagined LW · weight transfer through laces<span class="pos-tags"><span class="pos irb">IRB</span></span><span class="why">Trent's signature pass. As an inverted RB, switching from the right channel to the left winger is a high-value action you'll do 10+ times a match.</span></div><div class="scheme">8 reps</div></div>
          <div class="drill-line"><div class="name"><strong>Diagonal switch — left foot</strong> · same drill, opposite direction · simulate inverted LB role too<span class="pos-tags"><span class="pos both">BOTH</span></span><span class="why">Two-footed switches make you positionally flexible — you can play either inverted fullback role.</span></div><div class="scheme">8 reps</div></div>
          <div class="drill-line"><div class="name"><strong>Line-breaking through ball</strong> · driven low pass between two cones (defenders) · 20 yards · both feet<span class="pos-tags"><span class="pos irb">IRB</span></span></div><div class="scheme">10 reps</div></div>
        </div>

        <div class="session-block">
          <div class="block-head">
            <span class="block-num">BLOCK 04</span>
            <span class="block-title">1v1 Attacking from Wide</span>
            <span class="block-time">12 MIN</span>
          </div>
          <div class="drill-line"><div class="name"><strong>Cut-inside on right foot</strong> · LW position, defender (cone) on outside, chop inside, accelerate · the Salah / Mbappé pattern<span class="pos-tags"><span class="pos lw">LW</span></span><span class="why">Your bread and butter as a left winger. Eight reps before progressing — you want this automatic.</span></div><div class="scheme">8 reps</div></div>
          <div class="drill-line"><div class="name"><strong>Beat outside on left foot</strong> · LW position, defender shows you inside, push down the line on left · uses your LEFT as a weapon<span class="pos-tags"><span class="pos lw">LW</span></span><span class="why">Most "inverted" wingers can't do this — defenders force them inside because they're predictable. Two-footed gives you the option.</span></div><div class="scheme">8 reps</div></div>
          <div class="drill-line"><div class="name"><strong>Overlap + cross — RB lane</strong> · simulate getting forward as traditional RB, deliver cross on right foot<span class="pos-tags"><span class="pos irb">IRB</span></span><span class="why">Even as inverted RB, you'll have moments when you bomb forward. Don't lose this.</span></div><div class="scheme">6 reps</div></div>
        </div>

        <div class="session-block">
          <div class="block-head">
            <span class="block-num">BLOCK 05</span>
            <span class="block-title">Finishing — Position-Specific</span>
            <span class="block-time">10–15 MIN</span>
          </div>
          <div class="drill-line"><div class="name"><strong>Curling shot — left half-space</strong> · receive at 22 yds, take 1 touch inside, curl with right foot to far post<span class="pos-tags"><span class="pos lw">LW</span></span><span class="why">The exact shot Salah lives off. Top-bin or far post, both work — what matters is the shape and the consistency.</span></div><div class="scheme">10 reps</div></div>
          <div class="drill-line"><div class="name"><strong>Driven low strike — right half-space</strong> · LB position, take a touch forward, drive a low ball across goal<span class="pos-tags"><span class="pos lw">LW</span></span></div><div class="scheme">5 reps</div></div>
          <div class="drill-line"><div class="name"><strong>Long-range strike — both feet</strong> · 25-yard strikes, simulate IRB stepping into space and striking · 5 each foot<span class="pos-tags"><span class="pos irb">IRB</span></span><span class="why">Inverted fullbacks find space at the edge of the box during sustained possession. Reward the position with goals.</span></div><div class="scheme">10 reps</div></div>
          <div class="drill-line"><div class="name"><strong>1-touch finish off cross</strong> · self-cross from right wing (right foot), sprint, finish first-time on left foot<span class="pos-tags"><span class="pos both">BOTH</span></span><span class="why">As LW, this is the back-post finish off the cutback. As RB, this is the run you make on overlap.</span></div><div class="scheme">8 reps</div></div>
        </div>

        <div class="session-block">
          <div class="block-head">
            <span class="block-num">BLOCK 06</span>
            <span class="block-title">Cool-down</span>
            <span class="block-time">5 MIN</span>
          </div>
          <div class="drill-line"><div class="name"><strong>Light juggling</strong> · bring HR down, restore touch<span class="pos-tags"><span class="pos both">BOTH</span></span></div><div class="scheme">2 min</div></div>
          <div class="drill-line"><div class="name"><strong>Static stretch</strong> · hamstrings, calves, hip flexors, adductors<span class="pos-tags"><span class="pos both">BOTH</span></span></div><div class="scheme">3 min</div></div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="day-section coretrain">
        <div class="label">Rotational Power Core <span class="opt">opt</span> · 8 min · post-soccer</div>
        <div class="exercise-list">
          <div class="exercise-row"><span class="num">01</span><span class="name">Med Ball Rotational Throw<span class="detail">against wall, full hip drive · both directions equal</span></span><span class="equip">med ball + wall</span><span class="scheme">3 × 6/side</span></div>
