          <div class="block-head">
            <span class="block-num">BLOCK 01</span>
            <span class="block-title">Soccer Activation</span>
            <span class="block-time">10 MIN</span>
          </div>
          <div class="drill-line"><div class="name"><strong>Light dribble pattern</strong> · figure-8 around 2 cones, 8 yds apart, both feet<span class="pos-tags"><span class="pos both">BOTH</span></span></div><div class="scheme">4 min</div></div>
          <div class="drill-line"><div class="name"><strong>Wall passes — short range</strong> · prep for the runs ahead<span class="pos-tags"><span class="pos both">BOTH</span></span></div><div class="scheme">3 min</div></div>
          <div class="drill-line"><div class="name"><strong>Acceleration starts</strong> · 3-point start, 10 yards at 80%<span class="pos-tags"><span class="pos both">BOTH</span></span></div><div class="scheme">3 × 10 yds</div></div>
        </div>

        <div class="session-block">
          <div class="block-head">
            <span class="block-num">BLOCK 02</span>
            <span class="block-title">Defensive Footwork + 1v1 Defending</span>
            <span class="block-time">12 MIN</span>
          </div>
          <div class="drill-line"><div class="name"><strong>Defensive shuffle + close-out</strong> · backpedal 5 yds, shuffle laterally 5 yds, sprint forward 5 yds to close down<span class="pos-tags"><span class="pos irb">IRB</span></span><span class="why">The exact movement pattern when a winger receives wide and you're closing from the inside. Drill the footwork until it's automatic.</span></div><div class="scheme">8 reps</div></div>
          <div class="drill-line"><div class="name"><strong>Jockey + force outside</strong> · approach with body angled to force the attacker down the line · cone setup simulating winger receiving<span class="pos-tags"><span class="pos irb">IRB</span></span><span class="why">As an inverted RB you're often the only defender wide — never let them come inside. Body shape sells the position before the ball arrives.</span></div><div class="scheme">8 reps</div></div>
          <div class="drill-line"><div class="name"><strong>High-press chase</strong> · sprint 15 yards forward to "press" a stationary ball, decelerate, jockey<span class="pos-tags"><span class="pos lw">LW</span></span><span class="why">Modern wingers are the first line of defense. Get the jog-to-sprint trigger ingrained.</span></div><div class="scheme">8 reps</div></div>
          <div class="drill-line"><div class="name"><strong>Recovery sprint to wide channel</strong> · start central (inverted position), sprint 25 yds to outside cone (RB position), arrive ready<span class="pos-tags"><span class="pos irb">IRB</span></span><span class="why">The single biggest weakness of inverted fullbacks. When possession breaks, you have to GET BACK. This is that exact run.</span></div><div class="scheme">6 reps</div></div>
        </div>

        <div class="session-block">
          <div class="block-head">
            <span class="block-num">BLOCK 03</span>
            <span class="block-title">Repeat-Sprint Conditioning</span>
