    <p class="section-intro">Core for an inverted RB / left winger isn't crunches and planks for a six-pack — it's anti-rotation for jockeying, anti-extension to protect the lower back during sprinting and kicking, rotational power to drive your strikes and switches, and lateral chain strength for change-of-direction. Four routines, each tied to specific days. Stack what you have time for; the daily activation is the closest to non-negotiable.</p>

